ved_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzI3MzE4Mjcx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/crash","name":"crash","color":"885544","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-09-05T16:12:10Z","updated_at":"2025-09-06T19:23:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.5.beta.mono.double.custom_build [4ed8c45ab] (master)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta.mono.double (4ed8c45ab) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 9 7950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 31.11 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen loading in certain meshes on a build using `precision=double`, MeshDataTool will crash when trying to access the array of tangents. \n\nI was able to fix by changing `real_t` to `float` when reading tangents in the MeshDataTool but considering the rendering server supports `PACKED_FLOAT64_ARRAY` for tangents, I'm concerned this is not a valid general solution.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse `MeshDataTool.create_from_surface` in the attached MRP.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mesh-data-crash.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22175526/mesh-data-crash.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/g